(* README *)

1 - Description
    -----------

    T001 provides a mechanized proof of the “Carryless Pairing” construction in 
    Rocq. The development relies on the standard libraries Arith, List, Bool,
    and PeanoNat.

    `T001__Comprehension.v` packages the core definitions, the abstract
    correctness theorem, the concrete `P0` realizations, and the closed
    `P0` endpoint theorems into one audit-facing synopsis layer.

    `T001__QED.v` is the canonical QED surface for T001: it documents the
    Rocq criteria in `PROPOSITIO`, exposes a premise-free concrete
    `PROPOSITIO_P0`, discharges both endpoint layers in Q.E.D. by direct
    reuse of the correctness stack, and exposes the OCaml extraction surface
    for the concrete `P0` realization.

    The `appendix/` directory contains the proof-erasure outputs generated from
    the development.


2 - Repository Tree
    ---------------

    .
    ├── README
    │
    │      (This file.)
    │
    ├── T001__Comprehension.v
    │
    │      Audit/comprehension layer for the carryless pairing package.
    │
    ├── T001__QED.v
    │
    │      Canonical QED surface for T001. States and documents PROPOSITIO,
    │      certifies the proof obligations (Q.E.D.), and exposes the
    │      executable `P0` extraction interface.
    │
    ├── R01__Carryless_Pairing_Definitions.v
    │
    │      Core definitions of the carryless pairing function, including the
    │      arithmetic encoding, auxiliary constructions, and structural lemmas.
    │
    ├── R02__Carryless_Pairing_Correctness.v
    │
    │      Main correctness results. In particular, it proves 
    │      [ unpair (pair x y) = (x, y) ] under the stated Zeckendorf
    │      specification, together with supporting soundness and representation
    │      lemmas.
    │
    ├── R03__Carryless_Pairing_Examples.v
    │
    │      Concrete realizations and computational examples, including a greedy
    │      Zeckendorf construction and `vm_compute` evaluations.
    │
    ├── R04__Carryless_P0_Correctness.v
    │
    │      Concrete closure layer discharging the abstract Zeckendorf criteria
    │      for `P0` and deriving premise-free `unpair_pair_P0` / `pair_inj_P0`.
    │
    └── appendix
           ├── assumptions
           │       │
           │       ├── unpair_pair_QED.out
           │       ├── pair_inj_QED.out
           │       ├── carryless_pairing_QED.out
           │       ├── unpair_pair_P0_QED.out
           │       ├── pair_inj_P0_QED.out
           │       └── carryless_pairing_P0_QED.out
           │
           │              Redirect-generated Print Assumptions outputs for
           │              the abstract and concrete QED theorems.
           │
           ├── Carryless_Pairing.ml
           │
           └── Carryless_Pairing.mli

                  Generated OCaml interface exposing the extracted types and
                  functions.
